## Performance Optimization Tips

### 1. Use Zero-Copy Reads

```rust
// Instead of copying
let record = log.read(offset).await?;
let bytes = record.value.clone();  // Copy

// Use zero-copy
let record = log.read(offset).await?;
let bytes = &record.value;  // Reference
```

### 2. Reuse Buffers

```rust
// Instead of allocating each time
for event in events {
    let buffer = Vec::new();  // Allocates
    process(event, &mut buffer)?;
}

// Reuse buffer
let mut buffer = Vec::with_capacity(1024);
for event in events {
    buffer.clear();
    process(event, &mut buffer)?;
}
```

### 3. Batch Operations

```rust
// Instead of individual writes
for event in events {
    log.append(event).await?;  // Slow
}

// Batch writes
log.append_batch(events).await?;  // Fast
```

### 4. Use Async Effectively

```rust
// Instead of sequential
for event in events {
    process(event).await?;  // Sequential
}

// Process concurrently
let handles: Vec<_> = events
    .into_iter()
    .map(|e| tokio::spawn(process(e)))
    .collect();

for handle in handles {
    handle.await??;
}
```

